{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>As the woman's husband shall lay upon him</b> — when the husband sues him in court to impose a penalty for this. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 21:22), and it is correct. Similarly, \"as it shall seem good to you\" (Genesis 40:14), and many similar instances. And the meaning is that he is liable for the value of the children as the husband shall lay upon him, and not as the woman shall lay upon him, for she has no share or claim in them. But Onkelos (Onkelos on Exodus 21:22) translated: \"according to what they shall impose upon him.\" And Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] said: \"according to all that the woman's husband shall lay upon him, or he shall give by the judges\" — as though it said that he may reach a settlement with him by mutual agreement, or he shall pay their full value according to the court. This is not correct, for what reason is there to mention this? In my opinion, since there is no discernible injury to the children — for who knows whether they would have survived — Scripture said: even though there is no monetary compensation here, a penalty shall be imposed upon him, and it is like a fine or money that others impose upon him against his will. Similarly, \"and he laid a penalty upon the land\" (2 Kings 23:33), \"and they drink wine of those penalized\" (Amos 2:8). And it said that the penalty shall be according to all that the woman's husband shall lay upon him — for he desires his children, and they are valued by him — and he shall give this by the judges, so that he shall not impose a penalty upon him greater than their full value. And in the Mekhilta (here): \"'As he shall lay upon him' — might I understand [to mean] whatever he wishes? Scripture states, 'and he shall give by the judges,' and \"pelilim\" means nothing other than judges.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:13:35.564483952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}